    <briefdescription>
<para>Process-wide allocation counter used by <computeroutput><ref refid="class_stats_allocator" kindref="compound">StatsAllocator</ref></computeroutput> for debugging and benchmarking. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>All counters (<computeroutput><ref refid="class_alloc_logger_af7bf5fe7168d05a22c0e7b3fcf5bb14a_1af7bf5fe7168d05a22c0e7b3fcf5bb14a" kindref="member">mNumAllocs</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_alloc_logger_aa756006f79111b20bf10fcf1bc6e6439_1aa756006f79111b20bf10fcf1bc6e6439" kindref="member">mAllocSize</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_alloc_logger_a2e4e5e0ede8f97caac4e56d06247eaf1_1a2e4e5e0ede8f97caac4e56d06247eaf1" kindref="member">mNumDeallocs</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_alloc_logger_a6dd47aa0a04870e729d040d82b42cd5c_1a6dd47aa0a04870e729d040d82b42cd5c" kindref="member">mCurrentAllocSize</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_alloc_logger_ad3aec269607bbd4959bc902923cf8691_1ad3aec269607bbd4959bc902923cf8691" kindref="member">mHighWater</ref></computeroutput>) are <computeroutput>static</computeroutput>, so the logger tracks every <computeroutput><ref refid="class_stats_allocator" kindref="compound">StatsAllocator</ref></computeroutput>-mediated allocation in the process at once. <computeroutput><ref refid="class_alloc_logger_ab8baf7d79cc01fe70cd7969099f6bd67_1ab8baf7d79cc01fe70cd7969099f6bd67" kindref="member">logAlloc</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="class_alloc_logger_af9c6b46dbd1b16e054a09ebe9c6be0f9_1af9c6b46dbd1b16e054a09ebe9c6be0f9" kindref="member">logDealloc</ref></computeroutput> are called from the allocator hooks; <computeroutput><ref refid="class_alloc_logger_ac307252ec51609f133ab2e504d02f75a_1ac307252ec51609f133ab2e504d02f75a" kindref="member">reset()</ref></computeroutput> zeroes everything for a fresh measurement. Not thread-safe <mdash/> intended only for diagnostic runs. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
